---
title: State diagram - document (Document.Status, Document.IsArchived)
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    state "Pending<br>(awaiting review)" as Pending
    state "Approved" as Approved
    state "Rejected<br>(ReviewComment required)" as Rejected
    state "Archived<br>IsArchived = true (soft delete)" as Archived

    [*] --> Pending : POST /api/documents/upload, then POST /api/documents
    Pending --> Approved : PATCH /api/documents/{id}/status Approved
    Pending --> Rejected : PATCH status Rejected + comment
    Approved --> Rejected : PATCH status Rejected + comment
    Rejected --> Approved : PATCH status Approved
    Approved --> Pending : PATCH status Pending
    Rejected --> Pending : PATCH status Pending
    Pending --> Archived : DELETE /api/documents/{id}
    Approved --> Archived : DELETE /api/documents/{id}
    Rejected --> Archived : DELETE /api/documents/{id}
    Archived --> [*]

    note right of Rejected
        The client fixes a rejection by uploading a NEW copy
        (a new Document row in Pending, same case and type).
        The old row stays Rejected; the web hides it once a
        newer copy of the same type exists.
    end note

    note left of Pending
        Status changes: Admin, or the case's assigned
        consultant. Any status to any status is accepted;
        every change writes an AuditLog row.
        Archive: Admin or assigned consultant; again = 409.
        Archived is not a hard end: the status PATCH does
        not check IsArchived, and GET still returns the row.
    end note
